  overviewEyebrow:"01 — Original brief", overviewTitle:"Learning object-oriented design through a visual application", overviewLead:"The assignment consisted of developing a small browser-based 2D drawing application with HTML, CSS and TypeScript.", overviewText:"The user selects a colour, stroke width and figure type, then clicks in the drawing area to define its geometry. A point requires one click and a segment requires two. The application redraws all stored figures on an HTML Canvas and allows several figures of the same type to be created consecutively.", disclaimer:"This page is based on the original 29-page practical assignment found in my files. The final source folder and authentic screenshots are not currently available in the portfolio, so the three visuals below are clearly marked as temporary reconstructions.",
